          "fields": {
            "display_title": "In this work the authors tackle the problem of learning good, task-relevant representations for Reinforcement Learning (RL) with policy gradient (PG) methods. Specifically they propose combining the loss of a variational auto-encoder (VAE) with the PG loss during training to learn better features. They compare this approach against a pre trained VAE model with and without fine-tuning on the Atari Breakout task. ",
            "replying_to": "Replying to Guiding Representation Learning in Deep Generative Models with Policy Gradients"
